    "body": "Adds the first reconstructed standing resident to the1835Wolf Point yard, using the repaired Bardwell & Otis portable model. Connected waistcoat shoulders, shoes and source-bounded identity cards replace the earlier defects. The cards distinguish the reconstructed person and appearance from the historically modelled firm.\n\nThe canonical authoring/export remains source96c4da4b and successful run39736567239; all eight canonical GLBs, the placement, person data and1835runtime are unchanged through the final DEV integration. This is an initial standing example; full photographic likeness/tailoring, the rest of the modular library, other eras, walking, drivers and riders remain open underT-1789.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Current pushed head `b0924b41c25d0d9bf975feb9b6e245a1b3f288e3`, tree `5a6ad43ef2dda3fe002d2f5de3476fbba7927af6`, integrates DEV `59da1aaacc9af6bc07d362339ebee6ee62ed2d5c`.\n- Full preflight passed1,046 checks including381 self-tests. Postcommit publication and mirror passed:2,068 exact source files,3,140 declared transforms,zero unmapped.\n- Four fresh published smoke cells are running: parts14 and15 in both desktop/mobile viewports. They cover the incoming1904Kimball/Glessner and shared disclosure/arrival changes. Current normal CI is pending.\n- Actual person desktop/mobile source-head779visual/contact/selection checks passed; all eight PNGs were personally reviewed. Canonical export/source proofs and earlier broad smoke results retain their original commit labels. Final integration preserves their person/runtime dependencies; this is incremental coverage, not a claim that all18cells ran onb092.\n\nSupplemental desktop readiness stress attempts exceeded their original540/90-second limits and remain documented follow-up; they are not relabelled as passing. The newly appended release-note data passes the changelog/mirror contracts; the entire long part13 has not been rerun on this final head.\n\nDEV only. No production promotion, broad parent-ticket closure, occupied/ride interaction or photographic-completion claim. Recovery evidence is pushed in `kevinrhaas/chicago-tickets`, including `checkpoint-2f-pushed-and-horse0b` and `checkpoint-actual-horse-yard-and-v14-native`.\n",
